.TH CARLOS-CTL 8 "2026-09-03" "carlos-emr" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
carlos\-ctl \- administer a CARLOS EMR host installed from the carlos\-emr package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B carlos\-ctl
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B carlos\-ctl
is the administration interface for a single\-host CARLOS EMR deployment
installed from the
.B carlos\-emr
package.
.PP
The package's maintainer scripts call the same verbs an administrator does, so
provisioning logic exists in exactly one place: what
.B dpkg\-reconfigure
runs is what you can re\-run by hand, and it behaves identically.
.PP
Most commands require root.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Diagnosis
.TP
.B check
Run the full deployment check and exit non\-zero if anything fails. It verifies
that the services are running, that no component is running as root, that
Tomcat and MariaDB listen on loopback only, that the certificate is valid, that
the security response headers are served, that the WAF blocks a probe
SQL\-injection request, that DrugRef is not reachable through the front door,
that the schema has a Flyway history, and that backups are fresh. Start here.
.TP
.B status
Systemd status of the EMR, nginx, MariaDB and the package's timers.
.TP
.BR restart ", " start ", " stop
Service lifecycle passthroughs.
.B restart
is what applies configuration changes; expect about two minutes for the
webapp to redeploy.
.TP
.BR logs " [\fIjournalctl-args\fR]"
Application server log.
.SS Schema
.TP
.B db-info
Show which migrations are applied and which are pending.
.TP
.B db-validate
Verify the schema matches the migrations shipped in the deployed WAR. This is
the same check the application performs at boot.
.TP
.B db-migrate
Apply pending migrations.
.B Take a verified backup first:
DDL is not transactional in MariaDB and a failed migration can leave a
partially\-changed schema.
.TP
.B db-baseline
Adopt an existing pre\-Flyway (OSCAR 19 / OpenO) schema by stamping the history
at the full genesis, version 1.0.2. Follow it with
.BR db-migrate .
Never stamp at 1: Flyway would re\-run the province migrations, which DROP and
recreate province tables.
.TP
.B db-repair
Repair
.I flyway_schema_history
after a failed migration.
.TP
.B db-apply-settings
Restart MariaDB if — and only if — its running values disagree with the
packaged drop\-in (checked first, so an upgrade that changes nothing never
bounces the database).
.TP
.BR "db" " [\fIargs\fR]"
Raw mariadb client on the EMR database as root over the unix socket:
interactive with no arguments; client arguments and redirects pass through
(the same contract as the carlos\-podman tool's
.B db
verb).
.TP
.B db-dump
Write a consistent dump to standard output. It is never written to a default
path: a dump is the entire clinical record in one file and the operator must
choose, and secure, where it lands.
.SS Certificates
.TP
.B cert status
Show which certificate is being served and when it expires.
.TP
.BR "cert selfsigned" " [\fB\-\-force\fR]"
Generate the self\-signed pair, or regenerate it when it is within 30 days of
expiry.
.TP
.BI "cert acme " email
Obtain and install a Let's Encrypt certificate with certbot's webroot method.
Requires that
.B CARLOS_SERVER_NAME
resolves in public DNS to this host and that port 80 is reachable.
.TP
.B cert manual
Adopt a certificate chain and key you placed at
.I /etc/carlos\-emr/tls/fullchain.pem
and
.IR privkey.pem .
Nothing will overwrite them afterwards.
.SS Web application firewall
.TP
.B waf status
ModSecurity engine state and the location of the policy and exclusion files.
.TP
.BR "waf tail" " [\fIlines\fR]"
Show recent WAF blocks with the rule id, what it matched and the request URI \-
the information an exclusion needs.
.TP
.B waf detect-only
Stop blocking. For triage only; do not leave a system holding patient data in
this state.
.TP
.B waf blocking
Resume blocking.
.TP
.B waf reload
Apply hand\-edited policy or exclusion files. Config\-tested first; on
failure the running rules keep serving and the command says so.
.SS Backups
.TP
.B backup full
Take a backup now, by starting the same systemd unit the nightly timer runs —
so a manual run and a timer run are the identical code path, with the unit's
sandbox and its read capability. The job itself executes as the
.B carlos\-backup
user, never as root.
.TP
.B backup verify
Restore the newest dump into the scratch database and check that it loaded.
.TP
.B backup status
When the last backup and the last restore drill succeeded.
.TP
.BR "backup snapshots" " [\fIargs\fR]"
List the contents of the restic repository.
.TP
.BR "backup restic " \fIargs\fR
Raw restic passthrough with the repository location and passphrase loaded
from backup.env, running as the
.B carlos\-backup
user. This is what the documented restore procedure is built on
(\fBrestic restore latest \-\-tag db \-\-target ...\fR); a bare
.B restic
would not see the repository. Runs outside the timer unit's sandbox, so it
can also restore to paths the unit itself may not write.
.SS Provisioning
.TP
.B init-config
Re\-render AND APPLY the derived configuration from
.IR /etc/carlos\-emr/carlos\-emr.env :
the nginx fragments are regenerated, a stale self\-signed certificate is
refreshed, nginx is config\-tested and reloaded, and the tool states whether
an application restart is also needed. Only keys this package owns are
touched; every other line of
.I carlos.properties
is left alone.
.TP
.B bootstrap-admin
Replace the seeded
.B carlosdoc
administrator password and PIN with random values and write them to
.IR /etc/carlos\-emr/initial\-admin.txt .
The migrations seed that account with a hash published in the CARLOS source
repository, so this runs at install time by default.
.TP
.B db-users
Create the databases and the least\-privilege accounts (the verb name
matches carlos\-podman). Idempotent, and it preserves any password already
configured.
.TP
.B rotate
Rotate every generated database password and restart the application.
.SS Decommissioning
.TP
.BI "destroy-data --confirm " server-name
The ONLY supported way this software destroys clinical data. It DROPs the
EMR and DrugRef databases and deletes patient documents, heap dumps and
application logs (the empty directory skeleton is recreated so the still-
installed services keep working); backups survive unless
.B --including-backups
is also given, which additionally deletes /var/backups/carlos-emr and
SHREDS backup.env and carlos.properties \(em the restic passphrase and the
application AES key, precisely so a copied-off repository cannot be read.
After it, a reinstall (or restored escrow copies of those two files) is
required before the host can run the EMR or read any remaining backup.
It refuses to run while MariaDB is unreachable: a destruction that cannot
drop the databases does not start. Removing or purging the packages never does any of this. The
command refuses unless the host's own configured name is typed back to it.
.SS Clinic migration from OSCAR 19 (experimental)
Migration output should receive a technical review \(em verification
report, spot checks, UI smoke \(em before clinical use.
.TP
.B import-o19 (experimental)
Import an OSCAR 19 clinic backup into a STOCK initial deploy (a fresh
Flyway schema holding only its seed rows; anything else is refused with no
override). Inputs: either
.B --bundle
.I FILE
\(em one archive (.tar/.tar.gz/.tar.enc/.tar.gz.enc; .enc is
openssl password-based encryption, unlocked with
.BR --bundle-pass ;
the digest the clinic conveyed separately is checked with
.B --bundle-sha256
before the bundle is opened, because openssl enc has no integrity check of
its own)
holding the dump, the OscarDocument tar and oscar.properties at its root
\(em or the three
.BR --dump / --documents / --properties
flags.
.B --admin-user
names the break-glass administrator created before the seeded clinician is
removed. The clinic's role matrix is merged under CARLOS's seeded grants
(CARLOS wins on the same role and object, clinic rows append) and
clinic-custom roles receive the CARLOS-era privileges of the closest stock
role;
.B --role-template
.I CUSTOM=STOCK
(repeatable, case-insensitive) overrides that choice; the mapping is
recorded in the import ledger once it validates and bound once the backfill
has decided on it, after which a
.B \-\-resume
continues with it (a different mapping is then refused; before that a resume
may add or correct the flag). Blockers found by the built-in preflight
are cleared only by explicit
.B \-\-accept
sign-off flags, recorded in the report. The CARLOS service must be stopped
for a real run: a running
.B carlos\-emr
unit is refused (its startup writes rows the row-parity gate would reject).
.B \-\-dry-run
stages and reports without writing to the EMR schema (its
.B \-\-accept
flags are not recorded; it still runs the P0 gates, and it is refused over a
workspace whose import is in progress);
.B \-\-resume
continues an interrupted real import (required whenever a previous run left
state behind beyond a staged dump \(em state is never continued implicitly;
once the data copy has started, only the emptiness sweep is skipped on
resume);
.B \-\-restage
drops and re-restores the staging schema (clearing the recorded preflight
verdict);
.B \-\-cleanup
drops the staging schema and the throwaway staging account, removes the
extracted bundle, retires the run's ledgers, report and private files with a
.I .completed-<time>
suffix and keeps the o19_archive schema and
.I admin-credentials.txt
\(em allowed after verification or while nothing has been written to the
EMR schema, never on a mid-import workspace. The pre-import backup is taken
before the staged restore, which runs as a throwaway account limited to the
staging schema; a dump carrying USE or CREATE DATABASE statements is
refused.
.B \-\-dev-target
and
.B \-\-mariadb-arg
serve development databases only and are refused on a packaged host
.RB ( \-\-fixups-dir
points a development run at the data-fixup scripts the package installs
under /usr/share/carlos-emr/schema/o19-fixups). See
docs/oscar19-to-carlos-migration-plan.md and docs/o19-import-deb.md in the
source tree.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.BR \-\-bundle " FILE" ,
.BR \-\-bundle-pass " SPEC"
(openssl \-pass spec: file:PATH, env:VAR, fd:N, stdin),
.BR \-\-bundle-sha256 " HEX" ,
.BR \-\-bundle-cipher " NAME"
(default aes-256-cbc),
.BR \-\-bundle-openssl-opt " OPT"
(repeatable passthrough for legacy bundles, e.g. \-md then md5);
.BR \-\-dump " FILE" ,
.BR \-\-documents " FILE" ,
.BR \-\-properties " FILE" ;
.BR \-\-skip-documents
(needs
.BR "\-\-accept no-documents" );
.BR \-\-province " on|bc"
(must match the host's configured province; the import supports Ontario);
.BR \-\-admin-user " NAME" ;
.BR \-\-role-template " CUSTOM=STOCK" ;
.BR \-\-accept " CLASS" ;
.BR \-\-dry-run ,
.BR \-\-resume ,
.BR \-\-restage ,
.BR \-\-cleanup ;
.BR \-\-statement-timeout " SECONDS"
(bound every SQL statement of the import to this many seconds, MariaDB
max_statement_time; 0 = no bound, the default);
.BR \-\-dev-target ,
.BR \-\-mariadb-arg " ARG" ,
.BR \-\-fixups-dir " DIR" .
.PP
Sign-off classes for
.BR \-\-accept :
.B archived-forms
(patient data in removed modules becomes archive-only),
.B unknown-as-archive
(tables the manifest does not know are archived whole),
.B dropped-columns
(columns CARLOS dropped are shadow-captured),
.B olis-gone
(OLIS data is archive-only),
.B charset-repair
(double-encoded text is repaired per row),
.B no-documents
(import without the documents tree),
.B no-pre-backup
(no pre-import restic snapshot; required when backups are not configured),
.B unverified-bundle
(open a bundle whose digest was never conveyed),
.B carry-credentials
(the dump carries live OAuth consumer secrets or signing keys, copied
verbatim; rotate or verify them before go-live). Every class is recorded in
the report and survives \-\-resume.
.RE
.TP
.B o19-preflight (experimental)
Stage a dump and run only the capacity checks and the go/no-go feasibility
check; the exit status is the verdict (0 go, 1 acknowledgements required,
2 no-go) and 3 for any failure of the tool itself (unreachable server, bad
flags, refused dump, disk); nothing is recorded as a sign-off and a
workspace whose import is in progress is refused untouched. Options:
.BR \-\-bundle ,
.BR \-\-bundle-pass ,
.BR \-\-bundle-sha256 ,
.BR \-\-bundle-cipher ,
.BR \-\-bundle-openssl-opt ,
.BR \-\-dump ,
.BR \-\-properties ,
.BR \-\-province ,
.BR \-\-accept ,
.BR \-\-restage ,
.BR \-\-mariadb-arg ,
.BR \-\-dev-target
as for
.BR import-o19 .
For an assessment BEFORE backups are shipped, copy
/usr/lib/carlos-emr/carlos_ctl/o19_preflight.py to the OSCAR 19 server and
run it there standalone.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/carlos-emr/carlos-emr.env
Site settings: host name, listen address, province, time zone, heap.
.TP
.I /etc/carlos-emr/carlos.properties
Application configuration and the application's database credential.
.TP
.I /etc/carlos-emr/backup.env
Backup repository, passphrase and the read\-only database credential.
.TP
.I /etc/carlos-emr/tomcat/
Tomcat configuration for the CARLOS instance.
.TP
.I /etc/carlos-emr/modsecurity/
WAF policy and site exclusions.
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/sites-available/carlos-emr
The front door.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B check
exits non\-zero when any check fails. Other commands exit non\-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8),
.BR certbot (1),
.BR restic (1),
.BR mariadb (1)
.PP
